# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=scripts/tsan.supp).
#
# A lock-order inversion inside a third-party C library, between its own locks, all taken on
# PatchBox's main thread (nothing else in the process calls it), so it can't deadlock here:
# Berkeley DB, which libjack's metadata uses: one order reading a property, another closing the
# client. (libdbus had one too; SDL no longer loads it.)
deadlock:libdb-5.3.so
